{"id":"mahabharata-3-273","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":273,"title":"त्रिसप्तत्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 273 · Indrajit slain","summary":{"en":"Vibhishana revives the brothers with water from Kubera that lets them see the invisible, and Lakshmana slays Indrajit in battle. Mad with grief, Ravana resolves to kill Sita, but his minister Avindhya restrains him, and he calls for his chariot.","kn":"ಅದೃಶ್ಯವನ್ನು ಕಾಣಿಸುವ ಕುಬೇರನ ಜಲದಿಂದ ವಿಭೀಷಣನು ಸಹೋದರರನ್ನು ಎಚ್ಚರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಲಕ್ಷ್ಮಣನು ಯುದ್ಧದಲ್ಲಿ ಇಂದ್ರಜಿತನನ್ನು ಕೊಲ್ಲುತ್ತಾನೆ. ದುಃಖದಿಂದ ಹುಚ್ಚನಾದ ರಾವಣನು ಸೀತೆಯನ್ನು ಕೊಲ್ಲಲು ನಿಶ್ಚಯಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಮಂತ್ರಿ ಅವಿಂಧ್ಯನು ತಡೆಯುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಅವನು ರಥ ತರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"विभीषण कुबेर के उस जल से भाइयों को सचेत करते हैं जिससे अदृश्य दिखाई देता है, और लक्ष्मण युद्ध में इन्द्रजित को मार डालते हैं। शोक से उन्मत्त रावण सीता को मारने का निश्चय करता है, पर मन्त्री अविन्ध्य उसे रोकता है, और वह अपना रथ मँगवाता है।","te":"అదృశ్యాన్ని చూపించే కుబేరుని జలంతో విభీషణుడు సోదరులను తేరుకోబెడతాడు, లక్ష్మణుడు యుద్ధంలో ఇంద్రజిత్తును సంహరిస్తాడు. దుఃఖంతో ఉన్మత్తుడైన రావణుడు సీతను చంపాలని నిశ్చయిస్తాడు, మంత్రి అవింధ్యుడు అడ్డుకుంటాడు, అతడు రథం తెప్పిస్తాడు.","ta":"மறைந்தவற்றைக் காணச் செய்யும் குபேரனின் நீரால் விபீஷணன் சகோதரர்களை எழுப்ப, லக்ஷ்மணன் போரில் இந்திரஜித்தைக் கொல்கிறான். துயரால் வெறிகொண்ட ராவணன் ஸீதையைக் கொல்லத் தீர்மானிக்க, அமைச்சர் அவிந்த்யன் தடுக்க, அவன் தன் தேரை வரவழைக்கிறான்.","ml":"കുബേരന്റെ ജലംകൊണ്ട് വിഭീഷണൻ സഹോദരന്മാരെ ഉണർത്തുന്നു; അതിലൂടെ അദൃശ്യരെയും കാണാനാകുന്നു; യുദ്ധത്തിൽ ലക്ഷ്മണൻ ഇന്ദ്രജിത്തിനെ വധിക്കുന്നു. ദുഃഖത്താൽ ഭ്രാന്തനായ രാവണൻ സീതയെ കൊല്ലാൻ തീരുമാനിക്കുന്നു, പക്ഷേ മന്ത്രി അവിന്ധ്യൻ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ തടയുന്നു; പിന്നെ തന്റെ രഥം വിളിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.273; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"द्रौपदीहरणपर्व","titleEn":"Draupadiharana Parva (Abduction of Draupadi)","verses":[{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तावुभौ पतितौ दृष्ट्वा भ्रातरावमितौजसौ ।\nबबन्ध रावणिर्भूयः शरैर्दत्तवरैस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the two brothers of immeasurable energy fallen, Indrajit bound them again with arrows given by boons."}},{"n":2,"text":"तौ वीरौ शरजालेन बद्धाविन्द्रजिता रणे ।\nरेजतुः पुरुषव्याघ्रौ शकुन्ताविव पञ्जरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those two heroes, bound in the battle by Indrajit's net of arrows, tigers among men, looked like two birds in a cage."}},{"n":3,"text":"तौ दृष्ट्वा पतितौ भूमौ शतशः सायकैश्चितौ ।\nसुग्रीवः कपिभिः सार्धं परिवार्य ततः स्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing them fallen to the ground, covered with hundreds of arrows, Sugriva stood surrounding them with the monkeys."}},{"n":4,"text":"सुषेणमैन्दद्विविदैः कुमुदेनाङ्गदेन च ।\nहनूमन्नीलतारैश्च नलेन च कपीश्वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The monkey king was there with Sushena, Mainda, Dvivida, Kumuda, Angada, Hanuman, Nila, Tara, and Nala."}},{"n":5,"text":"ततस्तं देशमागम्य कृतकर्मा विभीषणः ।\nबोधयामास तौ वीरौ प्रज्ञास्त्रेण प्रबोधितौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Vibhishana, his work done, came to that place and woke the two heroes with the weapon called Prajna, and they were roused."}},{"n":6,"text":"विशल्यौ चापि सुग्रीवः क्षणेनोभौ चकार तौ ।\nविशल्यया महौषध्या दिव्यमन्त्रप्रयुक्तया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sugriva also, in a moment, freed both of arrows by the great herb Vishalya applied with divine mantras."}},{"n":7,"text":"तौ लब्धसंज्ञौ नृवरौ विशल्यावुदतिष्ठताम् ।\nगततन्द्रीक्लमौ चास्तां क्षणेनोभौ महारथौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Regaining consciousness, the two best of men stood up, free of arrows, and in a moment those two great chariot-warriors were rid of drowsiness and fatigue."}},{"n":8,"text":"ततो विभीषणः पार्थ राममिक्ष्वाकुनन्दनम् ।\nउवाच विज्वरं दृष्ट्वा कृताञ्जलिरिदं वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, son of Pritha, Vibhishana, seeing Rama, delight of the Ikshvakus, free of fever, said these words with joined hands:"}},{"n":9,"text":"अयमम्भो गृहीत्वा तु राजराजस्य शासनात् ।\nगुह्यकोऽभ्यागतः श्वेतात्त्वत्सकाशमरिंदम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Tamer of foes, a yaksha has come from the White Mountain to you, bringing water at the command of the king of kings."}},{"n":10,"text":"इदमम्भः कुबेरस्ते महाराजः प्रयच्छति ।\nअन्तर्हितानां भूतानां दर्शनार्थं परंतप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kubera, the great king, sends you this water, scorcher of foes, so that you can see hidden beings."}},{"n":11,"text":"अनेन स्पृष्टनयनो भूतान्यन्तर्हितान्युत ।\nभवान्द्रक्ष्यति यस्मै च भवानेतत्प्रदास्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whoever's eyes are touched with it, and whoever you give it to, will see beings that are hidden.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"तथेति रामस्तद्वारि प्रतिगृह्याथ सत्कृतम् ।\nचकार नेत्रयोः शौचं लक्ष्मणश्च महामनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rama said \"So be it,\" received the honored water and washed his eyes with it, and the great-minded Lakshmana did the same."}},{"n":13,"text":"सुग्रीवजाम्बवन्तौ च हनूमानङ्गदस्तथा ।\nमैन्दद्विविदनीलाश्च प्रायः प्लवगसत्तमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sugriva, Jambavan, Hanuman, Angada, Mainda, Dvivida, Nila, and most of the other best monkeys did also."}},{"n":14,"text":"तथा समभवच्चापि यदुवाच विभीषणः ।\nक्षणेनातीन्द्रियाण्येषां चक्षूंष्यासन्युधिष्ठिर ॥","meaning":{"en":"It happened as Vibhishana said: in a moment their eyes could see beyond the senses, Yudhishthira."}},{"n":15,"text":"इन्द्रजित्कृतकर्मा तु पित्रे कर्म तदात्मनः ।\nनिवेद्य पुनरागच्छत्त्वरयाजिशिरः प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Indrajit, having done his work and reported it to his father, hurried back to the head of the battle."}},{"n":16,"text":"तमापतन्तं संक्रुद्धं पुनरेव युयुत्सया ।\nअभिदुद्राव सौमित्रिर्विभीषणमते स्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he came on again, enraged and eager to fight, Lakshmana, on Vibhishana's advice, ran at him."}},{"n":17,"text":"अकृताह्निकमेवैनं जिघांसुर्जितकाशिनम् ।\nशरैर्जघान संक्रुद्धः कृतसंज्ञोऽथ लक्ष्मणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wanting to kill the victorious Indrajit before he had performed his daily rites, the angry and now conscious Lakshmana struck him with arrows."}},{"n":18,"text":"तयोः समभवद्युद्धं तदान्योन्यं जिगीषतोः ।\nअतीव चित्रमाश्चर्यं शक्रप्रह्लादयोरिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"A fight took place between the two eager for victory, extremely wonderful and astonishing, like the one between Indra and Prahlada."}},{"n":19,"text":"अविध्यदिन्द्रजित्तीक्ष्णैः सौमित्रिं मर्मभेदिभिः ।\nसौमित्रिश्चानलस्पर्शैरविध्यद्रावणिं शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Indrajit pierced the son of Sumitra with sharp arrows that tear vital parts, and Lakshmana pierced Ravana's son with arrows that burned like fire."}},{"n":20,"text":"सौमित्रिशरसंस्पर्शाद्रावणिः क्रोधमूर्छितः ।\nअसृजल्लक्ष्मणायाष्टौ शरानाशीविषोपमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Touched by Lakshmana's arrows, Ravana's son, dizzy with rage, loosed eight arrows like venomous snakes at Lakshmana."}},{"n":21,"text":"तस्यासून्पावकस्पर्शैः सौमित्रिः पत्रिभिस्त्रिभिः ।\nयथा निरहरद्वीरस्तन्मे निगदतः शृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hear from me how the hero, son of Sumitra, took away his life with three fire-touched arrows."}},{"n":22,"text":"एकेनास्य धनुष्मन्तं बाहुं देहादपातयत् ।\nद्वितीयेन सनाराचं भुजं भूमौ न्यपातयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With one he cut the bow-bearing arm from his body, with the second he dropped the other arm with its iron arrow on the ground."}},{"n":23,"text":"तृतीयेन तु बाणेन पृथुधारेण भास्वता ।\nजहार सुनसं चारु शिरो भ्राजिष्णुकुण्डलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the third, a bright arrow with a broad edge, he took off the lovely head with its fine nose and shining earrings."}},{"n":24,"text":"विनिकृत्तभुजस्कन्धं कबन्धं भीमदर्शनम् ।\nतं हत्वा सूतमप्यस्त्रैर्जघान बलिनां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"His body, with arms and shoulders cut off, was terrible to see; having struck it down, the best of the strong also killed his charioteer with weapons."}},{"n":25,"text":"लङ्कां प्रवेशयामासुर्वाजिनस्तं रथं तदा ।\nददर्श रावणस्तं च रथं पुत्रविनाकृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The horses then carried the chariot into Lanka, and Ravana saw that chariot without his son."}},{"n":26,"text":"स पुत्रं निहतं दृष्ट्वा त्रासात्संभ्रान्तलोचनः ।\nरावणः शोकमोहार्तो वैदेहीं हन्तुमुद्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his son killed, Ravana, eyes wild with terror, stunned with grief, set out to kill Sita."}},{"n":27,"text":"अशोकवनिकास्थां तां रामदर्शनलालसाम् ।\nखड्गमादाय दुष्टात्मा जवेनाभिपपात ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"That wicked one seized a sword and rushed at her, who was in the Ashoka grove, longing to see Rama."}},{"n":28,"text":"तं दृष्ट्वा तस्य दुर्बुद्धेरविन्ध्यः पापनिश्चयम् ।\nशमयामास संक्रुद्धं श्रूयतां येन हेतुना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the evil intent of that fool, Avindhya calmed him in his rage, for this reason; listen."}},{"n":29,"text":"महाराज्ये स्थितो दीप्ते न स्त्रियं हन्तुमर्हसि ।\nहतैवैषा यदा स्त्री च बन्धनस्था च ते गृहे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You stand in a blazing great kingdom; you should not kill a woman. She is already dead, as a woman bound in your house."}},{"n":30,"text":"न चैषा देहभेदेन हता स्यादिति मे मतिः ।\nजहि भर्तारमेवास्या हते तस्मिन्हता भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In my view she would not be killed by destroying her body. Kill her husband; when he is killed, she will be dead."}},{"n":31,"text":"न हि ते विक्रमे तुल्यः साक्षादपि शतक्रतुः ।\nअसकृद्धि त्वया सेन्द्रास्त्रासितास्त्रिदशा युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Not even Indra himself is your equal in valor; you have often terrified Indra and the gods in battle.\""}},{"n":32,"text":"एवं बहुविधैर्वाक्यैरविन्ध्यो रावणं तदा ।\nक्रुद्धं संशमयामास जगृहे च स तद्वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With such various words Avindhya calmed the angry Ravana then, and Ravana accepted them."}},{"n":33,"text":"निर्याणे स मतिं कृत्वा निधायासिं क्षपाचरः ।\nआज्ञापयामास तदा रथो मे कल्प्यतामिति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The night-wanderer, resolved to go out, put away his sword and ordered, \"Have my chariot readied.\""}}]}]}